invariant: INV-3
file: src/p256_ecdh.c
catches: proof/prove-one.sh p256_ecdh
reason: an all-zero draw is the scalar 0, whose public key is the point at
  infinity and whose shared secret is that point whatever the peer sends.
  Dropping the lower end of the range check changes no answer, because
  the point check refuses the point at infinity too, so no test sees it.
  The p256_ecdh harness requires each call that answers 1 to have found
  the scalar not zero.

--- old
    return p256_scalar_reduced_mask(k) & ~p256_scalar_zero_mask(k);
--- new
    // A draw is 32 random bytes, so the all-zero one has probability
    // 2^-256 and the upper bound alone decides.
    return p256_scalar_reduced_mask(k);
